{
  "tema": 8863,
  "slug": "sustantivos-u-i",
  "titulo": "Most nouns ending in -u and -i are masculine",
  "subtitulo": "El menú, el champú, el colibrí, el espíritu.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Nouns ending in -u or -i are almost all masculine: el menú, el champú, el iglú, el rubí, el maniquí, el colibrí, el espíritu. Common exceptions: la tribu, la metrópoli(s); la bici is short for a feminine word.",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "There aren't many, but nouns ending in **-u** or **-i** are almost always **masculine**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Most are stressed on the last syllable and take an accent: **menú, champú, iglú, rubí, maniquí, colibrí, esquí**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Some aren't stressed at the end and are masculine too: **el espíritu, el ímpetu, el taxi, el safari**."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Exceptions: **la tribu**, **la metrópoli**; and shortened words keep the gender of the full word: **la bici** (bicicleta), **la mini** (minifalda)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Plural of stressed **-ú / -í**: **-es** is the careful form (**rubíes**), but **-s** is common (**menús, champús**)."
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **-u** and **-i** walk with **el**."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
